      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Lydia Pell ran the pharmacy her grandfather built: steel shutters, a brass key for the dispensary and a ledger for every pill. When the county and then the Cordon came for the antifungals she signed them out line by line, kept back what she could for the town and locked it in the dispensary safe. Then she pulled the shutter down. Looters pried the loading-bay door a week later and never made it out of the stockroom. Lydia had already locked herself in the office with the RX key, a box of candles and the ledger, and written her apology in its margin. The hook behind the counter is empty because the key is still on her desk, and so is she.",
